{
  "about": "Director-chat replay cases (PLAN.md §6.1 'Prompt hygiene + replay'). Each case is one message to the director on a fixture scene: Harbour Lights Ep 1 scene `scene` (0-based), one shot per script block. Scene 0 is S01 action (wide, kitchen), S02 Nimal's line, S03 action, S04 Kamala's line. `expect.lane` may be a list of acceptable lanes; `expect.ops` must each be contained in some applied operation; `expect.no_ops` means nothing may change; `expect.memory` means a production rule was stored. `rules: true` cases must pass without a model (checked in CI by tests/services/director_chat/test_replay.py); every case is scored with --model. `split` keeps tuning cases apart from held-out ones: change prompts against `tune`, report `heldout`. Do not edit cases to make a change pass. `dialogue` replaces the scene's lines in order (the fixture script is Sinhala). A case may be a conversation: `turns` is a list of {person, model, expect} (the person's message, the real model's recorded answers for that turn by schema name plus `reply`, and what must hold) or {choose: {block, option}} (the person clicks a card). `sinhala-switch-loop` is the Scene 2 thread of 2026-11-01 (plan/2026-11-01c): the model answers are the ones it gave, so it runs without a key. Since Phase 4 the translator answers it: `dialogue_translation` is the translator's recorded answer (a `line_id` of #2 means the scene's third line). The Sinhala and Tamil in these cases are TEST FIXTURES written for the harness, not reviewed by a Sinhala or Tamil speaker; the 20-line review the plan asks for happens before the translator is turned on for real scenes. A case may carry `role` ({can_edit, can_edit_script}). The ten multi-turn cases of Phase 6 are from the Scene 2 thread and the failures around it (language switch, card then 'did you apply it?', confirm without a card, a request repeated, a role without rights).",
  "cases": [
    {"id": "retime-explicit", "split": "tune", "rules": true, "scene": 0,
